# The step of bv_make_2, the constructor of a BallVector with 2-limb centers (milestone2.md,
# "BallVector", "Values"): a center given as an Expansion<T, 2>, canonical already (finite and
# normalized, (+-inf, +-0) or two NaN), copied limb for limb. Its limbs were written through Kairn
# (stored), so rule R3 asks no guard; the constructors of kairn/ball_vector.hpp, whose centers the
# program supplies, call bv_center_entry_2, which guards each limb first. A center given as two
# arrays of limbs of the program's own that is not normalized is not covered: its step would be
# make_2_limbs, which has no real-model statement, and the step of a ball vector needs one.
kernel:        bv_center_2
input:         x = x0 x1
output:        z = z0 z1
value:         x
requires:      canonical x
ensures:       normalized z
ensures:       error z R c=0 k=2 t=0
ensures:       represents z
min_precision: 1
theorem:       proofs/theories/BvNegMake.v bv_center_2_correct
source:        a copy of a canonical pair (milestone2.md, BallVector, Values)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
status:        proved
domain:        extended
ieee_status:   proved
ieee_theorem:  proofs/theories/IeeeBvNegMake.v bv_center_2_ieee_correct
ieee_lead_theorem: proofs/theories/IeeeBvNegMake.v bv_center_2_ieee_lead
cone_exempt:   z1 = x1 does not reach z0; a copy is exact, and a non-finite x1 beside a finite x0 is not a canonical operand, so the finish of the constructor, which reads z0, stands in for the check

z0 = copy(x0)
z1 = copy(x1)
